ntdll: Take CPU features, gamepads and thread QoS from the host.

system.c reads the arm64 ID registers through sysctl, answers the
gamepad information class from the app's snapshot
(kitsune_gamepad_snapshot_v1) and stubs the battery. sync.c sets guest
threads' QoS class from the app's power mode with a yield backoff
(ios_qos_poll), and NtCreateEvent retries when it gets a -1 or 0
handle.
